STARS AND BARS

Given:
x1 + x2 + ... + xk = n


1. CASE: xi >= 0

Answer:
C(n + k - 1, k - 1)


2. CASE: xi >= 1

Subtract 1 from every variable:

yi = xi - 1

Then:
y1 + y2 + ... + yk = n - k

Answer:
C(n - 1, k - 1)


3. GENERIC CASE: xi >= p

Subtract p from every variable:

yi = xi - p

Then:
y1 + y2 + ... + yk = n - k*p

Apply Case 1:

Answer:
C(n - k*p + k - 1, k - 1)

Valid only when:
n >= k*p

Otherwise:
0 solutions.


KEY TRICK

Subtract the minimum p from every variable,
then apply the xi >= 0 formula.


QUICK REFERENCE

xi >= 0  ->  C(n + k - 1, k - 1)

xi >= 1  ->  C(n - 1, k - 1)

xi >= p  ->  C(n - k*p + k - 1, k - 1)